// Generated by scripts/seventyTwoAngels/assemble.ts from the OCR of
// Lazare Lenain, La Science Cabalistique (Angers, 1823), which is public
// domain. The French is that scan repaired; the English is translated from
// the repaired French. Neither draws on any modern published translation.
// Everything Lenain's four tables make derivable — degrees, dates, hours,
// decade, planet, choir — lives in seventyTwoAngelsDerived.ts, not here.
// See plan 031.
[
  "1st genius, Vehuiah והויה. His attribute is interpreted (God elevated and exalted above all things). He rules over the Hebrews. The name of God, according to this tongue, is named Jehovah. He governs the first ray of the Orient in the season of spring, that is to say the first five degrees of the sphere which begin on the 20th of March at midnight until the 24th inclusively, corresponding to the first decade of the sacred calendar, and to the first genius, named Chontaré, under the influence of Mars: this genius, and those that follow, up to the 8th, belong to the first order of angels that the orthodox call the choir of seraphim. He dwells in the region of fire; his sign is the ram, and he presides over the following five days: the 20th of March, the 31st of May, the 11th of August, the 22nd of October, and the 2nd of January; the invocation is made toward the Orient, from midnight precisely until twenty minutes past midnight, to obtain lights. It is by the virtue of these divine names that one becomes illuminated by the spirit of God; they must be pronounced at midnight precisely until twenty minutes past midnight, reciting the third verse of the 3rd psalm. (Et tu Domine susceptor meus et gloria mea et exaltans caput meum). One must have one's talisman prepared according to the principles of the cabalistic art. (See on this subject chapter 8.)\n\nThe person who is born under the influence of this genius has a subtle mind; they are endowed with great sagacity, passionate for the sciences and the arts, capable of undertaking and executing the most difficult things; they will love the military estate, because of the influence of Mars; they will have much energy, being dominated by fire.\n\nThe evil genius influences turbulent men; he governs promptness and anger.\n\n(1) See the book entitled la Théorèze, or the only Way of divine and human Sciences, edition of the year 7, page 226.",
  'Jeliel יליאל. Their attribute (God who succours). He governs Turkey (these peoples give God the name Aydy). His ray begins from the 6th degree up to the 10th, inclusively, corresponding to the influence of the genius named Asican (see the sacred calendar), and to the first decade. He presides over the following days: 21 March, 1 June, 12 August, 23 October, 3 January.\n\nThis genius is invoked to calm popular seditions, and to obtain victory over those who attack you unjustly. The request must be spoken with the name of the genius, and one must recite the 20th verse of psalm 21. (Tu autem Domine ne elongaveris auxilium tuum a me ad defensionem meam conspice). The favourable hour begins from twenty minutes past midnight until forty minutes past midnight.\n\nThis genius governs kings and princes; he keeps their subjects in obedience; he influences the generation of all beings that exist in the animal kingdom; he restores peace among spouses and conjugal fidelity. Those who are born under this influence have a cheerful spirit, agreeable and gallant manners; they are passionate for the opposite sex.\n\nThe contrary genius governs all that is harmful to living beings; he delights in disuniting spouses by drawing them away from their duties; he inspires a taste for celibacy and bad morals.',
  "Sitaël כיטאל. His attribute (God, the hope of all creatures.) His ray begins from the 5th degree of Aries up to the 15th., inclusively, corresponding to the second decade and to the genius named Chontacré, under the influence of the sun; he presides over the following days: the 22nd of March, 2nd of June, 13th of August, 24th of October, 4th of January.\n\nThis genius is invoked against adversities; the request is uttered with the divine names and the 2nd verse of psalm 90. (Dicet Domino: susceptor meus es tu et refugium meum: Deus meus, sperabo in eum.) The favourable hour begins from forty minutes past midnight until one o'clock. He governs nobility, magnanimity and great employments; he protects against weapons and ferocious beasts. They who are born under this influence love the truth; they will keep their word, and they will take pleasure in obliging those who shall have need of their services.\n\nThe contrary genius governs hypocrisy, ingratitude and perjury.",
  "Elemiah. His attribute is interpreted (Hidden God). He corresponds to the holy name of God Allah, according to the language of the Arabs. His ray begins from the 16th degree of the sphere up to the 20th, inclusively, corresponding to the second decade and to the genius named Sénacher. He presides over the following days: the 23rd of March, the 3rd of June, the 14th of August, the 25th of October, the 5th of January. This genius is invoked against torments of the spirit and to know traitors. The request must be spoken with the 4th verse of the 6th psalm. (Convertere Domine, et eripe animam meam: salvum me fac propter misericordiam tuam.) The favourable hour begins from one o'clock up to one o'clock twenty minutes.\n\nThis genius governs voyages, maritime expeditions, and he influences useful discoveries. The person who is born under this influence will be industrious, happy in their undertakings, and will be passionate for travel.\n\nThe contrary genius governs bad upbringing, discoveries dangerous to society; he brings hindrance into every undertaking.",
  'Mahasiah בוהשיה. His attribute (God the Savior). He corresponds to the holy name Teut or Theuth (1), according to the language of the Egyptians. His ray begins from the 21st degree up to the 25th, inclusively, corresponding to the third decade and to the genius named Seket, under the influence of Venus; he presides over the following five days: 24 March, 4 June, 14 August, 26 October, 6 January. The invocation is made from one hour twenty minutes until one hour forty.\n\nThis genius is invoked in order to live in peace with everyone; one must pronounce the divine names and the 4th verse of psalm 33. (Exquisivi Dominum, et exaudivit me: et ex omnibus tribulationibus meis eripuit me). He governs the high sciences, occult philosophy, theology and the liberal arts. The person who is born under this influence will learn all they desire with ease; they will have an agreeable countenance and character, and will be fond of honest pleasures.\n\nThe contrary genius governs ignorance, libertinism, and all the bad qualities of body and mind.',
  'Lelahel ללהאל. His attribute (God laudable). He corresponds to the name Abgd, according to the language of the Ethiopians. His ray begins from the 26th degree up to the 30th, inclusively, corresponding to the third decade and to the genius named Asentacer; he presides over the following days: 25 March, 5 June, 15 August, 27 October, 7 January. This genius is invoked to acquire enlightenment and to cure illnesses; one must recite the 11th verse of psalm 9. ( Psallite Domino, qui habitat in Sion : annuntiate inter gentes studia ejus.) The favourable hour begins from 1 hour 40 minutes until 2 hours. This genius governs love, fame, the sciences, the arts and fortune. The person who is born under this influence will love to be talked about, and they will acquire celebrity through their talents and their actions.\n\nThe contrary genius governs ambition; he leads men to wish to rise above others; he influences all those who seek to acquire fortune by illicit means.',
  "Achaiah אכאיה. His attribute (Good and patient God).\n\nHis ray begins from the 31st. degree of the sphere up to the 35°., inclusively, corresponding to the fourth decade and to the genius named Choüs, under the influence of Mercury. He presides over the following days: 26 March, 6 June, 16 August, 28 October, 8 January. The invocation is made from 2 o'clock in the morning until 2 o'clock 20 minutes. One must recite the 8th. verse of psalm 102. (Miserator et misericors Dominus, longanimis, et multum misericors.) This genius governs patience; he uncovers the secrets of nature; he has influence over the spread of learning and over industry. The person who is born under this influence will love to instruct themself in useful things; they will take pride in carrying out the most difficult works, and they will discover several processes useful to the arts.\n\nThe contrary genius is the enemy of learning; he gives negligence, laziness, and carelessness about study.",
  '8th. Cahethel כהת אל. attribute / Adorable God). He corresponds to the holy name Moti, according to the language of the Georgians. His ray begins from the 36th degree of the sphere up to the 40th, inclusively, corresponding to the fourth decade and to the genius named Asicat; he presides over the following days; the 27th of March, the 7th of June, the 17th of August, the 29th of October, the 9th of January. One invokes the help of this genius by pronouncing the 6th verse of psalm 94. (Venite adoremus, et procidamus : et ploremus ante Dominum, qui fecit nos.) It serves to obtain the blessing of God and to drive away evil spirits. This genius governs all agricultural produce, and principally that which is necessary to the existence of men and animals. He inspires man to raise himself towards God, to thank him for all the good things he sends upon the earth. The person who is born under this influence will love work, agriculture, the countryside and hunting, and they will have much activity in business.\n\nThe evil genius provokes everything that is harmful to the produce of the earth; he leads man to blaspheme against God.',
  "Haziel דדזיאל. His attribute (God of mercy). He corresponds to the holy name Agzi, according to the language of the Abyssinians. His ray begins from the 41st degree up to the 45th, inclusively, corresponding to the fifth decade and to the genius named Eró; under the influence of the moon. This genius and those that follow, up to the 16th, belong to the 2nd order of angels, which the orthodox call the choir of cherubim. He presides over the following days: 28 March, 8 June, 18 August, 30 October, 10 January. The invocation is made from 2 hours 40 minutes in the morning until 3 o'clock, reciting the 6th verse of psalm 24. (Reminiscere miserationum tuarum, Domine, et misericordiarum tuarum quæ à sæculo sunt.) He serves to obtain the mercy of God, the friendship and favours of the great, and the fulfilment of a promise made by a person. He governs good faith and reconciliation. Those who are born under this influence will be sincere in their promises, and will readily forgive those who have offended them.\n\nThe contrary genius governs hatred and hypocrisy; he influences all those who seek to deceive by every possible means; he makes enemies irreconcilable.",
  "109. Aladiah אלדיה. His attribute (God propitious). He corresponds to the divine names Siré and Eipi, according to the language of the Persians. His ray begins from the 41st degree up to the 50th, inclusively, corresponding to the decade and to the genius named Viroaso. He presides over the following days: March 29, June 9, August 19, October 31, January 11. The invocation is made from 3 o'clock in the morning until three hours 20 minutes, reciting the 22nd verse of psalm 32. (Fiat misericordia tua Domine super nos: quemadmodum speravimus in te.) He is good for those who have hidden crimes and who fear being discovered. This genius governs against rabies and the plague, and influences the healing of illnesses. The person who is born under this influence will enjoy good health, and they will be happy in their undertakings, esteemed by those who will know them; they will frequent the best society.\n\nThe contrary genius influences those who neglect their health and their affairs.",
  '11th. Lauviah לאויה. His attribute (God praised and exalted). He corresponds to the holy name Deus, according to the tongue of the Latins.\n\nHis ray begins from the 51st degree of the sphere up to the 55th, inclusively, corresponding to the 6th decade and to the genius named Rombomare, under the influence of Saturn. He presides over the following days: 30 March, 10 June, 21 August, 1 November, 12 January. The favourable hour begins from 3 hours 20 minutes until 3 hours 40 minutes. One recites the 50th verse of psalm 17. (Dominus et benedictus Deus meus, et exultatur Deus salutis meæ.)\n\nHe serves against lightning, and to obtain victory. This genius governs fame; he influences great personages, scholars, and all those who become celebrated through their talents.\n\nThe contrary genius governs pride, ambition, jealousy and calumny.',
  'Hahaiah הדעיה. His attribute is interpreted (God takes refuge.) He corresponds to the holy name Théos, according to the tongue of the Greeks. His ray begins from the 56th degree of the sphere up to the 60th, inclusively, corresponding to the 6th decade and to the genius named Atarph; he presides over the following days: March 31, June 11, August 22, November 2, January 13. One invokes the help of this genius against adversities; you shall pronounce the 22nd verse of psalm 9. (Ut quid Domine recessisti longé, despicis in opportunitatibus, in tribulatione.) The favourable hour begins from 3 hours 40 minutes until 4 hours. He grants dreams, and reveals mysteries hidden from mortals. He has influence over wise, spiritual and discreet persons. The person who is born under this influence has gentle manners, an amiable countenance, and agreeable ways.\n\nThe contrary genius governs indiscretion and lying; he has influence over all those who abuse the trust of persons.',
  "Iezalel ידלאל. His attribute (God glorified above all things). He corresponds to the holy name of God Boog, according to the tongue of the Illyrians. His ray begins from the 61st degree of the sphere unto the 65th, inclusively, corresponding to the 7th decade and to the genius named Théosolk, under the influence of Jupiter. He presides over the days following: the 1st of April, 12th of June, 23rd of August, 3rd of September, 14th of January. The favourable hour begins from 4 o'clock unto 4 o'clock 20 minutes. One must recite the 6th verse of psalm 97. (Jubilate Deo omnis terra: cantate, et exultate, et psallite.)\n\nHe governs friendship, reconciliation, and conjugal fidelity. The person who is born under this influence will learn all that they wish with facility; they will have a fortunate memory, and will distinguish themselves by their skill.\n\nThe contrary genius governs ignorance, error and falsehood, and works upon narrow minds who wish neither to learn nor to do anything.",
  "Mebahel כובהאל. His attribute (God the preserver). He corresponds to the holy name Dios, according to the Spanish tongue. His ray begins from the 66th degree up to the 70th, inclusively, corresponding to the 7th decade, and to the genius named Thésogar. He presides over the following days: 2 April, 13 June, 24 August, 4 November, 15 January. This genius is invoked against those who seek to usurp another's fortune; one must recite the 9th verse of psalm 9. (Et factus est Dominus refugium pauperis: adjutor in opportunitatibus, in tribulatione.) The favourable hour begins from 4 hours 20 minutes until 4 hours 40. He governs justice, truth and liberty; he delivers the oppressed and prisoners; he protects innocence and makes the truth known. The person who is born under this influence will love jurisprudence, and they will distinguish themselves at the bar.\n\nThe contrary genius governs slander, false witness and legal proceedings.",
  "Hariel הרואל. His attribute (God the creator). He corresponds to the divine names Idio or Iddio, according to the Italian tongue. His ray begins from the 71st degree up to the 75th, inclusively, corresponding to the 8th decade and to the genius named Ouéré, under the influence of Mars. He presides over the following days: 3 April, 14 June, 25 August, 5 November, 16 January. This genius is invoked against the impious in religion; one pronounces their names along with the divine names and the 22nd verse of psalm 2. (And the Lord is become my refuge: and my God the help of my hope.) The favourable hour begins from 4 hours 40 minutes until 5 o'clock. This genius governs the sciences and the arts; he influences useful discoveries and new methods. The person who is born under this influence will love the company of good people; they will have religious feelings, and they will distinguish themselves by the purity of their morals.\n\nThe contrary genius governs schisms, wars of religion; he influences the impious and all those who propagate dangerous sects, and who seek means of establishing new ones.",
  "16th. Hakamiah הקמויה. His attribute (God who erects the universe.) He rules over France, and corresponds to the name Dieu, according to the language of that nation. His ray begins from the 76th degree of the sphere up to the 80th, inclusively, corresponding to the 8th decade and to the genius named Vérasua, under the influence of Mars. He presides over the following days: 4 April, 15 June, 26 August, 6 November, 17 January. This genius is invoked against traitors, to obtain victory over the enemy, and to be delivered from those who wish to oppress us; one must pronounce their names along with what follows: O God all-powerful of armies, thou who erectest the universe, thou who protectest the French nation, I invoke thee, I, so-and-so, by the name of Hakamiah, that thou mayst deliver France from her enemies. You shall then pronounce the 1st mysterious verse of psalm 87. (Domine Deus salutis meæ, in die clamavi, et nocte coram te.) This prayer must be recited every day, the face turned toward the east, from 5 o'clock in the morning until 5 o'clock and 20 minutes. This genius rules over crowned heads and great captains; he gives victory, and prevents seditions; he has influence over iron, arsenals, and all that pertains to the genius of war. The man who is born under this influence is of a frank, loyal and brave character, sensitive on the point of honour, faithful to his oath, and passionate for Venus.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over traitors; he provokes betrayals, sedition and revolt.",
  "Lauviah לאייה. Their attribute (God admirable). He corresponds to the name Goth, according to the language of the Germans. His ray begins from the 81st degree of the sphere up to the 85th, inclusively, corresponding to the ninth decade and to the genius named Phuor, under the influence of the Sun. He presides over the following days: 5 April, 16 June, 27 August, 7 November, 18 January. This genius and those that follow up to the 24th belong to the 5th order of angels named the choir of thrones. The invocation is made, every day while fasting, from 5 o'clock in the morning until 5 o'clock 20 minutes: one must pronounce the 1st verse of psalm 8. (Domine Deus noster, quam admirabile est nomen tuum in universa terra! - O Lord our God, how admirable is thy name in all the earth!) He serves against torments of the spirit, sadness, and to rest well at night. He governs the high sciences, marvelous discoveries, and grants revelations in dream. The person who is born under this influence will love music, poetry, literature and philosophy.\n\nThe contrary genius governs atheism, impious philosophers and all those who attack the dogmas of religion.",
  "Caliel. כליאל His attribute is interpreted (God prompt to hear). He corresponds to the name Boog, according to the language of the Poles. His ray begins from the 86th. degree of the sphere up to the 90th., corresponding to the ninth decade and to the genius named Tepisatosoa; he presides over the following days, namely: the 6th of April, 17th of June, 28th of August, 8th of November, 19th of January. This genius is invoked to obtain prompt help when some adversities arise; one must recite the 9th. verse of psalm 7. (Judica me Domine secundum justitiam meam, et secundum innocentiam meam super me.) The favourable hour begins from five hours 40 minutes in the morning until 6 o'clock. This genius makes truth known in legal proceedings, he makes innocence triumph, he confounds the guilty and false witnesses. The person who is born under this influence will be just and upright, will love the truth, and they will distinguish themselves in the magistracy.\n\nThe contrary genius governs scandalous lawsuits, he influences vile, base and grovelling men, and those who seek to muddle affairs and to enrich themselves at the expense of their clients.",
  "19th Leuviah לויה. His attribute (God who hears sinners). He corresponds to the name Bogy, according to the tongue of the Hungarians. He governs the first ray of the south, which begins from the 91st degree of the sphere up to the 95th, inclusively, corresponding to the tenth decade and to the genius named Sotis, under the influence of Venus; he presides over the following days: the 7th of April, the 18th of June, the 29th of August, the 9th of November, the 20th of January. One invokes the help of this genius toward midday, from 6 o'clock in the morning until 6 hours 20 minutes, reciting the 1st verse of psalm 39. (Expectans expectavi Dominum, et intendit mihi.) He serves to obtain the grace of God. This genius governs the memory and the intelligence of man. The person who is born under this influence shall be amiable and cheerful, modest in their words, and simple in their manner of being, they shall bear adversities with resignation and much patience.\n\nThe contrary genius has influence over sorrows, losses, and mortifications; he provokes debauchery and despair.",
  '20*. Pahaliah םס5 פהליה. attribute (God the redeemer).\n\nHe corresponds to the holy name Tios, according to the language of the Muscovites. His ray begins from the 95th degree of the sphere up to the 100th, inclusively, corresponding to the tenth decade and to the genius named Sothis; he presides on the 8th of April, 19th of June, 30th of August, 10th of November, 21st of January, which correspond to the influence of Venus. (See the sacred calendar, page 41.) The invocation is made from 6 hours 20 minutes until 6 hours 40 minutes; one must recite the 2nd verse of psalm 119. (Domine libera animam meam à labiis iniquis, et à linguâ dolosâ.) He serves against the enemies of religion, and to convert peoples to Christianity. This genius governs religion, theology and morals; he influences chastity and piety, and those whose vocation is for the ecclesiastical state.\n\nThe contrary genius governs irreligion, apostates, libertines and renegades.',
  'Nelchael נלכאל. His attribute (God alone and unique). He corresponds to the name Bueg, according to the language of the Bohemians. His ray begins from the 101st degree of the sphere up to the 105th, inclusively, corresponding to the 11th decade and to the genius named Sith, under the influence of Mercury. He presides over the following days: 9 April, 20 June, 31 August, 11 November, 22 January. The invocation is made from 6 hours 40 minutes in the morning until 7 hours. One must pronounce the 18th verse of psalm 30. (Ego autem in te speravi Domine : dixi Deus meus es tu : in manibus tuis sortes meæ.) He serves against slanderers, charms, and to destroy the power of evil spirits. This genius governs astronomy, mathematics, geography, and all the abstract sciences; he influences scholars and philosophers. The person who is born under this influence will love poetry, literature, and will be passionate about study; they will distinguish themselves in mathematics and geometry.\n\nThe evil genius governs ignorance, error and prejudice.',
  "corresponds to the holy name Good, according to the English tongue. His ray begins from the 106th degree of the sphere up to the 110th, inclusively, corresponding to the 11th decade and to the genius named Sith, under the influence of Mercury. He presides over the following days: 10 April, 21 June, 1 September, 12 November, 22 January. The invocation is made from seven o'clock until 7 hours 20 minutes; one pronounces the 16th verse of psalm 120. (Dominus custodit te; Dominus protectio tua, super manum dexteram tuam.) This genius governs fortune, renown, diplomacy and commerce; he has influence over travels, discoveries, and maritime expeditions; he protects against storms and shipwrecks. The person who is born under this influence will love commerce, will be industrious, and they will be distinguished by their liberal and philanthropic ideas.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over pirates, corsairs and slaves; he has influence over maritime expeditions.",
  'Melahel, attribute (God who delivers from evils). He corresponds to the name Dieh, according to the language of the Hibernians. His ray begins from the 111th degree of the sphere up to the 115th inclusively, corresponding to the 12th decade and to the genius named Chumis, under the influence of the Moon. He presides over the following days: 11 April, 22 June, 2 September, 13 November, 24 January. The invocation is made from 7 hours 20 minutes in the morning until 7 hours 40, reciting the 8th verse of psalm 120. (Dominus custodiat introitum tuum, et exitum tuum: et ex hoc nunc, et in sæculum.) He serves against weapons, and for travelling safely. This genius governs water, all the productions of the earth, and especially the plants that are necessary for the healing of illnesses. The person who is born under this influence is of a bold nature, and capable of undertaking the most perilous expeditions; they will distinguish themselves by honourable actions.\n\nThe contrary genius influences everything that is harmful to vegetation; he causes illnesses and plague.',
  "24. Hahiuiah ההויה. His attribute (God good in Himself). He corresponds to the holy name Esar, according to the language of the Etruscans. His ray begins from the 116th degree of the sphere up to the 120th, inclusively, corresponding to the 12th decade and to the genius named Thuimis. He presides over the following days: 12 April, 23 June, 3 September, 14 November, 25 January. The invocation is made from 7 o'clock 40 minutes in the morning until 8 o'clock: one pronounces the divine names with the 18th verse of psalm 32. (Ecce oculi Domini super metuentes eum: et in eis, qui sperant in misericordia ejus.) He serves to obtain the grace and mercy of God. This genius rules over exiles, fugitive prisoners, those condemned in absentia; he prevents the discovery of secret crimes, and those who have committed them will escape the justice of men, provided they do not fall again into the same fault; he protects against harmful animals, and he preserves from thieves and murderers. Those who are born under this influence love truth, the exact sciences; they are sincere in their words and their actions.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over all harmful creatures; he drives men to commit crimes, and has influence over all those who seek to live by unlawful means.",
  "Nith-Haiah נתהיה. Its attribute (God who gives wisdom.) He corresponds to the holy name of God Orsy, according to the language of the Magi. His ray begins from the 121st. degree of the sphere up to the 125th., inclusively, corresponding to the 13th. decade and to the genius named Charcumis, under the influence of Saturn. This genius and those that follow, up to the 32nd., belong to the 4th order of angels, whom the orthodox call the choir of dominations. He presides over the following days: 13 April, 24 June, 4 September, 15 November, 26 January. The invocation is made from 8 o'clock until 8 o'clock 20 minutes; you shall pronounce the divine names with the 1st. verse of psalm 9. (Confitebor tibi Domine in toto corde meo: narrabo omnia mirabilia tua.) He serves to gain wisdom, and to discover the truth of hidden mysteries. This genius governs all the occult sciences; he gives revelations in dreams, and particularly to those who are born on the day over which he presides; he influences wise men who love peace and solitude, and those who seek truth and practise the magic of the wise, which is that of God (1).\n\nThe contrary genius governs black magic, which is that of the evil principle, the demon; it consists in making a pact with him, whereby one pledges to renounce God, to do harm to men, to animals, and to the produce of the earth.\n\n(1) Modern philosophers call it the Science of Christ and of man.",
  "26. Haaiah האאיה. Their attribute (Hidden God), He corresponds to the holy divine names, Agdy and Abdi, according to the language of the Saracens. His ray begins from the 126th degree up to the 130th, inclusively, corresponding to the 13th decade, under the genius named Aphruimis. He presides over the following days: 14 April, 25 June, 5 September, 16 November, 27 January. The invocation is made from 8 hours 20 minutes in the morning until 8 hours 40. One must pronounce the divine names and the 145th verse of psalm 118. (Clamavi in toto corde meo, exaudi me Domine; justificationes tuas requiram.) He serves to win one's lawsuit and to make judges favourable to oneself. This genius protects all those who seek the truth; he leads men to the contemplation of divine things; he governs politics, diplomats, plenipotentiaries, ambassadors, treaties of peace and commerce, and all conventions in general: he has influence over couriers, dispatches, agents and secret expeditions.\n\nThe contrary genius governs traitors, the ambitious, and conspiracies.\n\n(1)",
  '27*. Ierathel ירתאל. His attribute (God who punishes the wicked). He corresponds to the holy name Téos, according to the language of the Copts. His ray begins from the 131st degree of the sphere up to the 135th, inclusively, corresponding to the 14th decade, and to the genius named Hépé, under the influence of Jupiter. He presides over the following days: April 15, June 26, September 6, November 17, January 28. The invocation is made from 8 hours 40 minutes in the morning until 9 hours. One pronounces the divine names and the 1st verse of psalm 139. (Eripe me Domine ab homine malo, a viro iniquo eripe me;) He serves to confound the wicked and slanderers, and to be delivered from our enemies. This genius protects against those who provoke and attack us unjustly. He governs the propagation of enlightenment, civilization and liberty. They who are born under this influence will love peace, justice, the sciences and the arts, and will distinguish themselves in literature.\n\nThe contrary genius governs ignorance, slavery and intolerance.',
  "28th. Seheiah שאהיה. His attribute (God who heals the sick). He corresponds to the holy name (1) Adad, according to the language of the Assyrians. His ray begins from the 136th degree up to the 140th, exclusively, corresponding to the 14th decade and to the genius named Sithacer. He presides over the following days: 16 April, 27 June, 7 September, 18 November, 29 January. The invocation is made from 9 o'clock in the morning until 9 o'clock 20 minutes. The divine names must be pronounced with the 15th verse of Psalm 70. (Deus ne elongeris à me : Deus meus in auxilium meum respice.) He serves against infirmities and thunder. This genius protects against fires, the ruin of buildings, falls, illnesses, etc. He governs health and longevity of life. The person who is born under this influence will have much judgment; they will act only with prudence and circumspection.\n\nThe contrary genius governs catastrophes, accidents, and causes apoplexies; it influences persons who never reflect before acting.",
  '29th. Renel רייאל. His attribute (God who is prompt to help) and corresponds to the holy name Zimi, according to the language of the Peruvians. His ray begins from the 141st degree of the sphere up to the 145th., inclusively, corresponding to the 15th. decade and to the genius named Phupé, under the influence of Mars. He presides over the following days: 17 April, 28 June, 8 September, 19 November, 30 January. The invocation is made from 9 hours 20 minutes in the morning until 9 hours 40. One must pronounce the divine names with the request and the 4th. verse of psalm 53. (Ecce enim Deus adjuvat me : et Dominus susceptor est animæ meæ.) He serves against the impious and the enemies of religion, and to be delivered from all enemies both visible and invisible. This genius governs all religious sentiments, divine philosophy and meditation. The person who is born under this influence will be distinguished by their virtues and their zeal for propagating the truth; they will make every effort to destroy impiety through their writings and by their example.\n\nThe contrary genius governs fanaticism and hypocrisy; he influences all those who propagate irreligion through writings and dangerous maxims.',
  "30. Omael. ומאאל His attribute (God patient.) He corresponds to the name Tura, according to the language of the Indians. His ray begins from the 146th degree of the sphere up to the 150th, inclusively, corresponding to the 9th decade and to the genius named Phuonisié. He presides over the following days: 28 April, 29 June, 9 September, 20 November, 31 January. The invocation is made from 9 hours 40 minutes in the morning until 10 o'clock: one pronounces the divine names and the 6th verse of psalm 70. (Quoniam tu es patientia mea Domine : Domine spes mea à juventute mea) He serves against sorrows, despair, and to have patience. This genius governs the animal kingdom; he watches over the generation of beings, so as to multiply their species and perpetuate their races; he influences chemists, physicians and surgeons. The person who is born under this influence will distinguish themselves in anatomy and medicine.\n\nThe contrary genius is the enemy of the propagation of beings; he influences monstrous phenomena.",
  "31st, Lecabel לכבאל. His attribute (God who inspires.) He corresponds to the holy name Teli, according to the language of the Chinese. His ray begins from the 151st degree up to the 155th, corresponding to the 16th decade and to the genius named Tomi, under the influence of the Sun. He presides over the following days: 19 April, 30 June, 10 September, 21 November, 1 February. One invokes the aid of Lecabel to obtain enlightenment, and for useful methods in the profession one practises. The invocation is made from 10 o'clock in the morning until 10 hours 20 minutes. One must utter the request with the divine names and the 16th mysterious verse of psalm 70. (Quoniam non cognovi litteraturam, introibo in potentias Domini: Domine memorabor justitiae tuae solius). He governs vegetation and agriculture. The person who is born under this influence will love astronomy, mathematics and geometry; they will be distinguished by their luminous ideas, and will solve the most difficult problems, and will owe their fortune only to their talents.\n\nThe contrary genius governs avarice and usury; he influences all those who enrich themselves by illicit means.",
  '32*. Vasariah ושריה. His attribute (Just God.) He corresponds to the name Anot, according to the language of the Tartars. His ray begins from the 156th degree of the sphere up to the 160th, inclusively, corresponding to the 16th decade and to the genius named Thumis. He presides over the following days: 20 April, 1 July, 11 September, 22 November, 2 February: One invokes the aid of this genius against those who attack us in court (1), and to obtain the mercy of those who have recourse to the clemency of kings; for this purpose one must name the person who attacks you, and state the reason; then pronounce the divine names with the 4th verse of psalm 32. (Quia rectum est verbum Domini, et omnia opera ejus in fide.) The favorable hour begins from 10 hours 20 minutes in the morning until 10 hours 40. This genius governs justice; he has influence over the nobility, jurisconsults, magistrates and lawyers. The person who is born under this influence will have a good memory and will speak with ease, they will be amiable, witty and modest.\n\nThe contrary genius governs all the bad qualities of the body and of the soul.',
  '33rd. Ilehuiah יהויה. His attribute (God who knows all things.) He corresponds to the holy name Agad, according to the language of the Hesperides. His ray begins from the 161st. degree of the sphere up to the 165th., inclusively, corresponding to the 17th. decade and to the genius named Ouestucati, under the influence of Venus. He presides over the following days: 21 April, 2 July, 12 September, 23 November, 5 February. This genius and those that follow, up to the 40th., belong to the 5th. order of angels, which the orthodox call the choir of powers. The invocation is made from 10 hours 40 minutes until 11 hours; one must pronounce the 11th. verse of psalm 33. (Dominus scit cogitationes hominum quoniam vanæ sunt.) He serves to know traitors, to destroy their plans and their machinations. This genius protects all Christian princes; he maintains their subjects in obedience. They who are born under this influence will love to fulfil all the duties of their station.\n\nThe contrary genius rules all insubordinate beings; he provokes the seditious to revolt.\n\n(1) If the attacked person recognises in their soul and conscience that they are in the wrong, they must accordingly invoke this genius, to come to an amicable arrangement with the adverse party, without which they would not succeed.',
  "Lehahiah לההיה. Its attribute (Merciful God.) It corresponds to the name Aneb, according to the language of the peoples of the Congo. Its ray begins from the 166th degree of the sphere up to the 170th, inclusively, corresponding to the 17th decade and to the genius named Thopitus. He presides over the following days: April 22, July 5, September 13, November 24, February 4. The invocation is made from 11 o'clock in the morning until 11 hours 20 minutes, reciting the verse of psalm 130. (Speret Israel in Domino; ex hoc nunc, et usque in seculum.) He serves against the genius who rules over crowned heads, princes and nobles; he maintains harmony, good understanding and peace among them; he influences the obedience of subjects toward their princes. The person who is born under this influence will become celebrated for their talents and their actions; they will have the confidence and favors of their prince, which they will earn by their devotion, their fidelity, and the great services they will render him.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over discord; he provokes war, betrayals, and the ruin of nations.",
  'Chavakiah כוקיה. His attribute (God who gives joy.) He corresponds to the name Anup. His ray begins from the 171st degree up to the 175th, inclusively, corresponding to the 18th decade and to the genius named Aphoso, under the influence of Mercury. He presides over the following days: 23 April, 4 July, 14 September, 25 November, 5 February.\n\nOne invokes the help of this genius to return to favor with those one has offended; for this purpose one must pronounce the request, the divine names, and name the person; then you shall say the 1st verse of psalm 114. (Dilexi, quoniam exaudiet Dominus vocem orationis meæ.) It must be recited every day, until you are reconciled with the person. The favorable hour begins from 11 hours 20 minutes in the morning until 11 hours 40. This genius governs wills, inheritances, and all divisions of property made amicably; he maintains peace and harmony within families. The person who is born under this influence loves to live in peace with everyone, even at the expense of their own interests; they make it a duty to reward the fidelity and good care of those who are attached to their service.\n\nThe contrary genius causes discord in family arrangements; he provokes unjust and ruinous lawsuits.',
  "36°, Menadel מנדאל. attribute (adorable God). He corresponds to the holy name Alla, according to the language of the Moors. His ray begins from the 176th degree of the sphere up to the 180th, inclusively, corresponding to the 18th decade and to the genius named Aphut. He presides over the following five days: 24 April, 5 July, 15 September, 26 November, 6 February. This genius is invoked to remain in one's employment, and to preserve the means of existence one possesses: the request is spoken along with the divine names and the 8th verse of psalm 25. (Domine dilexi decorem domus tuæ : et locum habitationis gloriæ tuæ.) He serves against calumnies and to deliver prisoners. The favourable hour begins from 11 hours 40 minutes in the morning until noon precisely. This genius gives insight concerning distant persons from whom one has received no news for a long time; he brings exiles back into their homeland, and discovers goods that have been lost or misappropriated.\n\nThe contrary genius protects all those who seek to flee abroad to escape justice.",
  '37*. Aniel אנואל. Their attribute (God of virtues). He corresponds to the holy name of God Abda, according to the ancient Philosophers. His ray begins from the 181st degree of the sphere up to the 185th, inclusively, corresponding to the 19th decade and to the genius named Souchoé, under the influence of the Moon. He presides over the following days: 25 April, 6 July, 16 September, 27 November, 7 February. The invocation is made from noon until twenty minutes past noon; one pronounces the divine names and the 8th verse of psalm 79. (Deus ad virtutem converte nos: et ostende faciem tuam et salvi erimus.) He serves to gain victory and to raise the siege of a town. This genius governs the sciences and the arts; he reveals the secrets of nature, and inspires wise philosophers in their meditations. The person born under this influence will acquire celebrity through their talents and their learning, and they will be distinguished among the learned.\n\nThe contrary genius governs perverse spirits; he influences charlatans and all those who excel in the art of deceiving men.',
  "Haamiah העביה. His attribute (God, the hope of all the children of the earth). He corresponds to the great name of God Acta \\baR (God threefold and one). According to the cabalists, this name is drawn from that mysterious verse of Scripture, אתה גיבר לעולם אדני, which signifies in French: Thou art the strong God through eternity (1). It is composed of the first letters of these four words, beginning from right to left (2). The ray of this genius begins from the 186th degree of the sphere up to the 190th, inclusively, corresponding to the 19th decade and to the genius named Serucuth. He presides over the following days: 26 April, 7 July, 17 September, 28 November, 8 February. These divine names are invoked to acquire all the treasures of heaven and earth; one must recite the 9th verse of psalm 90. (Quoniam tu es Domine spes mea: altissimum posuisti refugium tuum.) The cabalists say that this psalm serves against lightning, weapons, fierce animals, and infernal spirits. (See the cabala of the psalms.) This genius governs all religious cults, and everything relating to God; he protects all those who seek the truth.\n\nThe contrary genius governs error and lying, and influences all those who have no principle of religion.\n\n(1) See Agrippa, in the 3rd book of his Occult Philosophy, p. 41. At The Hague, 1727. It is likewise found in Kircher, Œdipus Ægyptiacus, volume 2, p. 113.\n\n(2) By this means you have the key to the 72 Hebrew verses that are written around the talismans of the 72 genii, which are found in the cabalistic sphere. Each of these verses contains the name of God and the attribute of the genius to which it corresponds. The abbé de Villars tells marvellous things, speaking of the great name AGLA, in his work entitled the Comte de Gabalis (see the third conversation). The best edition is that of Amsterdam, at Jacques Lejeune's, in 1700. He assures that with this name one works an infinity of wonders, even when pronounced by a profane mouth; he claims that those who wish to be convinced of the truth must exalt their imagination and their faith, then turn toward the east, observing on this subject everything that is indicated in the cabalistic rite.\n\nThe wise philosophers say that this name was revealed to Jacob, when he saw in a dream the ladder of 72 rungs, with the 72 angels who went up and down toward the place called the gate of heaven, and they claim that it is by it that Joseph was delivered from his brothers, and that he interpreted dreams, notably that of Pharaoh.\n\nThe cabalists write this name on the mysterious wand that is used in cabalistic experiments, and here is how it is made: one must cut a branch grown that same year, from a virgin hazel or filbert tree, that is to say the tree must never have borne fruit, and no branch must ever have been cut or broken, which is easily found in a shrub of new growth; it is cut between eleven and twelve o'clock at night, under influences favourable to the experiment one wishes to perform; one must have a new knife, that has never been used, and draw it upward while cutting the wand, and pronounce certain words, the face turned toward the east; then it must be blessed, and on the thicker end must be written the name AGLA, on the middle...",
  "Rehael רהעאל. His attribute (God who receives sinners). He corresponds to the holy name Goot, according to the language of the Scots. His span begins from the 191st degree of the sphere up to the 195th, inclusively, corresponding to the 20th decade and to the genius named Ptéchout, under the influence of Saturn. He presides over the following days: 27 April, 8 July, 18 September, 29 November, 9 February. The invocation is made from twelve forty until one o'clock. One must recite the 13th verse of psalm 29. (Audivit Dominus, et misertus est mei: Dominus factus est meus adjutor.) He serves for the healing of illnesses and for obtaining God's mercy. This genius governs health and length of life; he has influence over paternal and filial love, and over the obedience and respect of children toward their parents.\n\nThe contrary genius is named Terre-Morte or Terre-Damnée, according to the expression of Etteilla, in his Philosophie des Hautes-Sciences, page 83. He is the most cruel and the most treacherous genius known; he has influence over infanticides and parricides.",
  "40. Ieiazel. ייאל. His attribute (God who rejoices). He corresponds to the holy name Goed, according to the language of the Belgians. His ray begins from the 196th degree of the sphere up to the 200th, inclusively, corresponding to the 20th decade and to the genius named Aterchinis. He presides over the following five days: 28 April, 9 July, 19 September, 30 November, 10 February. The invocation is made from 1 o'clock in the afternoon until 1 o'clock 20 minutes. One pronounces the request with the divine names and the 15th verse of psalm 87. (Ut quid Domine repellis... faciem tuam à me.) This psalm has 5 marvelous properties; it serves to deliver prisoners, to obtain consolations, and to be delivered from one's enemies. This genius governs printing and bookselling; he influences men of letters and artists. The person who is born under this influence will love reading, drawing, and all the sciences in general.\n\nThe evil genius governs all the bad qualities of the body and the soul; he influences gloomy spirits and those who flee society.",
  "41. Hahahel הההאל. His attribute (God in three persons). He corresponds to the holy name Gudi, according to the Irish tongue. His ray begins from the 201st degree of the sphere up to the 205th, inclusively, corresponding to the 21st decade and to the genius named Chontaré, under the influence of Jupiter. He presides over the following days: 29 April, 10 July, 20 September, 1 December, 11 February. This genius and those that follow, up to the 48th, belong to the 9th order of angels, which the orthodox call the choir of Virtues. This genius is invoked (1) from 1 o'clock 20 minutes in the evening until 1 o'clock 40, by pronouncing the 2nd verse of psalm 119. (Domine libera animam meam à labiis iniquis, et à linguá dolosá.) He serves against the enemies of religion, the impious, and slanderers. This genius governs Christianity; he protects missionaries and all the disciples of Christ, who announce the words of the Gospel to the nations; he has influence over pious souls, prelates, ecclesiastics, and over all that pertains to the priesthood. The person who is born under this influence will be distinguished by their greatness of soul and their energy; they will devote themselves entirely to the service of God, and will not fear to suffer martyrdom for Christ.\n\nThe contrary genius influences apostates, renegades, and all those who dishonor the priesthood by their scandalous conduct.\n\n(1) Note that those who have recourse to this genius in their prayers must pay close attention to his attribute and his influence; for if you make to him a request contrary to his attributes, it will not succeed.",
  "42nd. Mikael מיכאל. The cabalists give him the following attributes: virtue of God, house of God, similar to God. He corresponds to the name Biub or Biud, according to the language of the Canadians. His ray begins from the 206th degree of the sphere up to the 210th inclusively, corresponding to the 21st decade and to the genius named Arpien. He presides over the following days: 30 April, 11 July, 21 September, 2 December, 12 February. The invocation is made from 1 hour 40 minutes until 2 o'clock exactly; one pronounces the request with the divine names and the 7th verse of psalm 120 (Dominus custodit te ab omni malo; custodiat animam tuam Dominus.) He serves for travelling safely. This genius influences monarchs, princes and nobles; he maintains their subjects in obedience, uncovers conspiracies, and all those who seek to destroy their persons and their governments. The person who is born under this influence will occupy themselves with political affairs; they will be curious, will wish to know the secrets of cabinets and foreign news, and they will distinguish themselves in affairs of state by their knowledge of diplomacy.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over traitors; he influences malevolence, and all those who spread false news.",
  "43. Veualiah ווליה. His attribute (Sovereign ruler). He corresponds to the holy name Solu, according to the language of the Californians. His ray begins from the 211th degree of the sphere up to the 215th, inclusively, corresponding to the 22nd decade and to the genius named Stochéné, under the influence of Mars. He presides over the following days: 1 May, 12 July, 22 September, 3 December, 13 February. The invocation is made from 2 o'clock in the afternoon until 2 hours 20 minutes, pronouncing the 14th verse of psalm 87. (Et ego ad te, Domine, clamavi: et mane oratio mea praeveniet te.) He serves to destroy the enemy and to be delivered from slavery. This genius presides over peace, and influences the prosperity of empires; he strengthens tottering thrones and the power of kings. The person who is born under this influence will love the military life and glory; they will occupy themselves constantly with the sciences that are connected with the genius of war; they will become famous through their feats of arms, and will earn the confidence of their prince through the services they render him.\n\nThe evil genius sows discord among princes; he influences the destruction of empires; he fosters revolutions and factional spirits.",
  '44*. Lelahiah ילהיה. His attribute (Eternal God). He corresponds to the holy name Bosa, according to the language of the Mexicans. His ray begins from the 216th degree of the sphere up to the 220th, inclusively, corresponding to the 22nd decade and to the genius named Sentacer. He presides over the following days: 2 May, 13 July, 23 September, 4 December, 14 February. This genius is invoked to obtain the success of a useful undertaking; the request must be pronounced with the divine names and the 108th verse of psalm 118, (Voluntaria oris mei bene placita fac Domine : et judicia tua doce me.) He is good for having the protection of magistrates and for winning a lawsuit. This genius protects against weapons; he gives victory. The person who is born under this influence will love to travel in order to learn, and all their undertakings will succeed; they will distinguish themselves by their military talents and their bravery, and their name will become celebrated in the annals of glory.\n\nThe contrary genius presides over war, and causes all the scourges that follow from it; he has influence over all those who violate the terms of surrender and massacre their prisoners without pity.',
  'Sealiah סאליה. His attribute (Mover of all things.) He corresponds to the holy name Hobo, according to the language of the peoples of Quito. His ray begins from the 221st degree of the sphere up to the 225th, corresponding to the 23rd decade and to the genius named Sesmé, under the influence of the Sun. He presides over the following days: 3 May, 14 July, 24 September, 5 December, 15 February. The invocation is made from 2 hours 40 minutes in the evening until 3 hours. One must pronounce the 18th verse of psalm 93. (Si dicebam, motus est pes meus: misericordia tua Domine adjuvabat me.) He serves to confound the wicked and the proud; he raises up those who are humbled and fallen. This genius governs vegetation; he carries life and health into all that breathes, and influences the principal agents of nature.\n\nThe person who is born under this influence will love to learn; they will have great means and much facility,\n\nThe contrary genius governs the atmosphere; he provokes great heats or great colds, great droughts or excessive humidity.',
  "Ariel מסם עריאל. attribute (God the revealer). He corresponds to the holy name Pino, according to the language of the peoples of Paraguay. His ray begins from the 226th degree of the sphere up to the 230th, inclusively, corresponding to the 23rd decade and to the genius named Tépiseuth. He presides over the following days: 4 May, 15 July, 25 September, 6 December, 16 February. This genius is invoked to obtain revelations; the request is spoken with the names and the 9th verse of psalm 144. (Suavis Dominus universis: et miserationes ejus super omnia opera ejus.) It serves to thank God for the goods he sends us. The favourable hour begins from 3 o'clock in the evening until 5 hours 20 minutes. This genius uncovers hidden treasures; he reveals the greatest secrets of nature, and he causes one to see in dream the objects one desires. The person who is born under this influence is endowed with a strong and subtle spirit; they will have new ideas and sublime thoughts; they will succeed in resolving the most difficult problems; they will be discreet and act with much circumspection.\n\nThe contrary genius causes tribulations of spirit; it leads men to commit the greatest inconsistencies, and influences weak minds.",
  'Asaliah עשליה. His attribute (Just God, who indicates the truth). He corresponds to the name Hana, according to the language of the peoples of Chile. His ray begins from the 231st degree up to the 235th, inclusively, corresponding to the 24th decade and to the genius named Siémé, under the influence of Venus. He presides over the following days: 5 May, 16 July, 26 September, 7 December, 17 February. The invocation is made from 3 hours 20 minutes in the afternoon until 3 hours 40, pronouncing the 25th verse of Psalm 104. (How great are thy works, O Lord! thou hast made all things in wisdom: the earth is filled with thy possession.) He serves to praise God and to raise oneself toward him when he sends us enlightenment. This genius rules over justice, and makes truth known in legal proceedings; he has influence over upright men, and over those who elevate their minds to the contemplation of divine things. They who are born under this influence are endowed with an agreeable character; they will be passionate about acquiring secret knowledge.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over immoral and scandalous actions, and over all those who propagate dangerous and chimerical systems.',
  '48. Mihael תספ בויהאל. attribute (God, helpful father).\n\nHe corresponds to the holy name Zaca (1), according to the language of the Japanese. His ray begins from the 236th degree of the sphere up to the 240th, inclusively, corresponding to the 24th decade and to the genius named Senciner. He presides over the five days following: 6 May, 17 July, 27 September, 8 December, 18 February. The invocation is made from 5 hours 40 minutes in the evening until 4 hours, pronouncing the 3rd verse of psalm 97. (Notum fecit Dominus salutare suum: in conspectu gentium revelavit justitiam suam.) He serves to preserve peace and union between spouses. This genius protects those who have recourse to him; they shall have premonitions and secret inspirations about all that shall befall them. He governs the generation of beings, and he has influence over friendship and conjugal fidelity. The person who is born under this influence shall be passionate about love; they shall love walking and pleasures in general.\n\nThe contrary genius governs luxury, sterility and inconstancy; he sets discord between spouses, and he causes jealousy and unease.',
  "49th. Vehuel והואל. His attribute (God great and exalted). He corresponds to the holy name of God Mara, according to the language of the inhabitants of the Philippine islands. His ray begins from the 241st degree of the sphere up to the 245th, inclusively, corresponding to the 25th decade and to the genius named Réuo, under the influence of Mercury. He presides over the following five days: 7 May, 18 July, 28 September, 9 December, 19 February. This genius and those that follow, up to the 56th, belong to the 7th order of angels, which the orthodox call the choir of principalities. The invocation is made from 4 o'clock in the evening until 4 o'clock 20 minutes; one pronounces the request with the divine names and the 3rd verse of psalm 144. (Magnus Dominus et laudabilis nimis et magnitudinis ejus non est finis.) One must recite this psalm entirely when one experiences sorrows and when one's spirit is troubled. It serves to exalt oneself toward God, to bless and glorify him, when one is moved by admiration. This genius governs great personages, and all those who rise up and distinguish themselves by their talents and their virtues. The person who is born under this influence will have a sensitive and generous soul; they will be esteemed by all people of good will for their virtues and their good deeds; they will distinguish themselves in literature, jurisprudence and diplomacy.\n\nThe contrary genius influences selfish men; he governs hatred and hypocrisy.",
  'Daniel דניאל. His attribute (the Sign of mercies), and according to others, the Angel of confessions (1). He corresponds to the holy name Pola, according to the language of the Samaritans. His ray begins from the 246th degree of the sphere up to the 250th, inclusively, corresponds to the 25th decade and to the genius named Eregbuo. He presides over the following days: May 8, July 19, September 29, December 10, February 20. The invocation is made from 4 hours 20 minutes in the evening until 4 hours 40 minutes, reciting the 8th verse of Psalm 102. (Miserator et misericors Dominus : longanimis et misericors.) He serves to obtain the mercy of God, and to have consolations. This genius rules over justice, lawyers, attorneys, and all magistrates in general. He gives inspiration to those who are embarrassed about several things, and do not know which one they ought to decide upon. The person who is born under this influence will be industrious and active in business; they will love literature, and they will distinguish themself by their eloquence.\n\nThe contrary genius influences swindlers, and all those who do not like work and seek to live by illicit means.\n\n(1) Kircher, Œdipus Ægyptiacus, volume 2, pages 266 and 267.',
  "Hahasiah ההשיה. His attribute (Hidden God). He corresponds to the holy name of God Bila, according to the language of the Barsians. His ray begins from the 251st degree of the sphere up to the 255th, inclusively, corresponding to the 26th decade and to the genius named Sesmé, under the influence of the Moon. He presides over the following five days: 9 May, 20 July, 30 September, 11 December, 21 February. The invocation is made from 4 hours 40 minutes until 5 o'clock, pronouncing the 32nd verse of psalm 103. (Sic: gloria Domini in sæculum : lætabitur Dominus in operibus suis.) He serves to raise the soul to the contemplation of divine things, and to discover the mysteries of wisdom. This genius rules over chemistry and physics; he reveals the greatest secrets of nature, notably the philosopher's stone and the universal medicine. The person who is born under this influence will love the abstract sciences; they will attach themselves particularly to knowing the properties and virtues attributed to animals, plants, and minerals; they will distinguish themselves in medicine by their marvelous cures, and they will make several discoveries useful to society.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over charlatans, and over all those who abuse people's good faith by promising them extraordinary things.",
  "Imamiah עכוכויה. His attribute (God elevated above all things). He corresponds to the name Abag, according to the language of the Melindais. His ray begins from the 256th degree of the sphere up to the 260th, inclusively, corresponding to the 26th decade and to the genius named Sagen. He presides over the five days following: 10 May, 21 July, 1 October, 12 December, 22 February. The invocation is made from 5 o'clock in the evening until 5 hours 20 minutes, reciting the 18th verse of psalm 7. (Confitebor Domino secundum justitiam ejus: et psallam nomini Domini altissimi.) He is good for destroying the power of enemies and for humbling them. This genius governs all journeys in general; he protects prisoners who have recourse to him; and inspires in them the means to obtain their liberty; he influences all those who seek the truth in good faith, and return from their errors by a very sincere turning back to God.\n\nThe person who is born under this influence will have a strong and vigorous temperament; they will bear adversities with much patience and courage; they will love work and will carry out all they wish with ease.\n\nThe contrary genius governs pride, blasphemy and wickedness; he influences coarse and quarrelsome men.",
  'His attribute (God who abases the proud). He corresponds to the holy name Obra (1), according to the language of the Maltese. His ray begins from the 261st degree of the sphere up to the 265th, inclusively, corresponding to the 27th decade and to the genius named Chommé, under the influence of Saturn. He presides over the following days: 11 May, 22 July, 2 October, 13 December, 23 February. The invocation is made from 5 hours 20 minutes in the evening until 5 hours 40 minutes, pronouncing the divine names with the 75th verse of psalm 118. (Cognovi Domine quia æquitas judicia tua : et in veritate tua humiliasti me.) This psalm is divided into 22 equal parts, corresponding to the 22 Hebrew letters and to the 22 sacred names of God, which correspond to each of these letters, and which indicate the ladder by which the wise ascend to the contemplation of God. The cabalists claim that the Holy Virgin recited it every day (see the Cabala of the Psalms). This genius governs the high sciences; he influences ecclesiastics, professors, magistrates, and men of law. They who are born under this influence will have a melancholic humor; they will love private life, rest and meditation; and they will distinguish themselves by their knowledge in the abstract sciences.\n\nThe contrary genius governs ignorance and all the bad qualities of body and of soul.\n\n(1) Sacred name according to the language of the Maltese.',
  "645. Nithael ניתאל. His attribute (King of the heavens). He corresponds to the holy name Bora, according to the language of the Zaflanians. His ray begins from the 266th degree of the sphere up to the 270th, inclusively, corresponding to the 27th decade and to the genius named Chénon. He presides over the following five days: 12 May, 23 July, 3 October, 14 December, 24 February. The invocation is made from 5 hours 40 minutes in the evening until 6 o'clock precisely, pronouncing the 19th verse of psalm 102 (Dominus in cælo paravit sedem suam: et regnum ipsius omnibus dominabitur.) He serves to obtain the mercy of God and to live long. This genius rules over emperors, kings, princes, and all civil and ecclesiastical dignities. He watches over legitimate dynasties, and over the stability of empires; he grants a long and peaceful reign to princes who have recourse to him, and protects all those who wish to maintain themselves in their positions. The person who is born under this influence will become famous for their writings and their eloquence; they will have much reputation among the learned, will distinguish themself by their virtues and will merit the confidence of their prince.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over the ruin of empires; he causes revolutions and upheavals; he has influence over all those who work toward the overthrow of monarchies in order to seize authority and the highest offices.",
  "Mebahiah בובהיה. His attribute (Eternal God). He corresponds to the name Alay, according to the language of the peoples of Ormuz. His ray begins from the 271st degree of the sphere up to the 275th, inclusively, corresponding to the 28th decade and to the genius named Smat, under the influence of Jupiter. He presides over the five days following: 13 May, 24 July, 4 October, 15 December, 25 February. The invocation is made from 6 o'clock in the evening until 6 hours 20 minutes; one pronounces the request with the divine names and the 13th verse of psalm 101. (Thou, Lord, remainest for ever: and thy memorial unto all generations). He is good for obtaining consolations, and for those who desire to have children. This genius governs morality and religion; he influences those who protect it with all their power, and propagate it by every possible means. The person who is born under this influence will distinguish themselves by their good deeds, their piety, and by their zeal in fulfilling their duties towards God and men.\n\nThe contrary genius is the enemy of truth; he influences all those who wish to destroy religion and the princes who protect it, in order to hinder the great work of the regeneration of mankind.",
  "Poiel 56. His attribute (God who sustains the universe). He corresponds to the holy name Illi, according to the language of the people of Aden. His ray begins from the 276th degree of the sphere up to the 280th, inclusively, corresponding to the 28th decade and to the genius named Themeso. He presides over the following days: 14 May, 25 July, 5 October, 16 December, 26 February. The invocation is made from 6 o'clock 20 minutes in the evening until 6 o'clock 40; One must pronounce the 15th verse of psalm 144. (Allevat Dominus omnes qui corruunt: et erigit omnes elisos.) He serves to obtain what one asks for. This genius governs fame, fortune and philosophy. The person who is born under this influence will be esteemed by everyone for their modesty, their moderation and their agreeable temper; they will owe their fortune only to their talents and their conduct.\n\nThe contrary genius governs ambition and pride: he influences all those who set themselves up as masters and wish to rise above others.",
  "Nemamiah נכומיה. His attribute (Praiseworthy God). He corresponds to the holy name Popa, according to the language of the Cyrenians. His ray begins from the 281st degree of the sphere up to the 285th, inclusively, corresponding to the 29th decade and to the genius named Sró, under the influence of Mars. He presides over the five days following: 15 May, 26 July, 6 October, 17 December, 27 February. This genius and those that follow, up to the 63rd, belong to the 8th order, which the orthodox call the choir of archangels. The invocation is made from 6 hours 40 minutes in the evening until 7 o'clock, reciting the 19th verse of psalm 113. (Qui timent Dominum speraverunt in Domino: adjutor eorum et protector eorum est.) He serves to prosper in all things, and to deliver prisoners. This genius governs great captains, admirals, generals, and all who fight for a just cause. They who are born under this influence will love the military life; they will be distinguished by their activity, their bravery and their greatness of soul, and they will bear hardships with much courage.\n\nThe contrary genius governs betrayals, causes discord among leaders; he influences cowardly men, and those who attack persons without defense.",
  "Teialel מסם יילאל. attribute (God who hears the generations). He corresponds to the holy name Para, according to the language of the Elamites. His ray begins from the 286th. degree of the sphere up to the 290th., inclusively, corresponding to the 29th. decade and to the genius named Epima. He presides over the following five days: 16 May, 27 July, 7 October, 18 December, 28 February. The invocation is made from 7 o'clock in the evening until 7 hours 20 minutes,\n\nOne pronounces the divine names and the 39th. verse of psalm 6. (Et anima turbata est valde; sed tu Domine usque quo?) He serves against sorrows and heals illnesses, principally the disease of the eyes (1). This genius governs iron; he has influence over armourers, locksmiths, cutlers, and all those who trade in it; he confounds the wicked and false witnesses. The person who is born under this influence will be distinguished by their bravery and their frankness, and they will be passionate for Venus.\n\nThe contrary genius governs anger; he has influence over the wicked and murderers.",
  'His attribute (God who knows all things). He corresponds to the holy name of God Ella, according to the language of the Mesopotamians. His ray begins from the 291st degree of the sphere up to the 295th, inclusively, corresponding to the 30th decade and to the genius named Isrô, under the influence of the Sun. His days are the following: 17 May, 28 July, 8 October, 19 December, 1 March. The favourable hour begins at 7 hours 20 minutes and lasts until 7 hours 40; one must pronounce the name of the genius, with his attributes, and the 3rd verse of psalm 112 (A solis ortu usque ad occasum, laudabile nomen Domini.) He is invoked against the sterility of women, and to render children submissive and respectful toward their parents. This genius governs treasures, stockbrokers, public funds, archives, libraries, and all rare and precious collections; he has influence over printing, bookselling, and over all who trade therein. The person who is born under this influence will love to instruct themselves in all the sciences in general; they will conduct much business, will follow the operations of the stock exchange, will speculate with advantage, and will distinguish themselves by their probity, their talents and their fortune.\n\nThe contrary genius is the enemy of enlightenment; he causes ruin and destruction through fires; he has influence over dilapidations and fraudulent bankruptcies.\n\n(1) See on this subject the Enchiridion of pope Leo, page 4.-',
  '60*. Mitzrael. His attribute (God who relieves the oppressed). He corresponds to the holy name Géna, according to the language of the peoples of Tibet. His ray begins from the 296th degree of the sphere up to the 300th, inclusively, corresponds to the 30th decade and to the genius named Homoth. He presides over the following days: 18 May, 29 July, 9 October, 20 December, 2 March. The invocation is made from 7 hours 40 minutes in the evening until 8 hours, pronouncing the 18th verse of psalm 144. (Justus Dominus in omnibus viis suis: et sanctus in omnibus operibus suis.) He serves to heal diseases of the spirit, and to be delivered from those who persecute us; he governs illustrious persons who distinguish themselves by their talents and their virtues; he influences the fidelity and obedience of subordinates toward their superiors. The person who is born under this influence will unite all the fine qualities of body and soul; they will distinguish themselves by their virtues, their wit, their agreeable temper, and they will live long.\n\nThe contrary genius governs all insubordinate beings, and influences all bad physical and moral qualities.',
  "Umabel ומבאל. His attribute (God above all things). He corresponds to the name Sila, according to the language of the ancient Bethulians. His ray begins from the 301st degree to the 305th, inclusively, corresponding to the 31st decade and to the genius named Ptiau, under the influence of Venus. He presides over the following days: 19 May, 30 July, 10 October, 21 December, 3 March. The invocation must be made from eight o'clock in the evening until 8 o'clock 20 minutes; one pronounces the divine names and the 2nd verse of psalm 112. (Sit nomen Domini benedictum, ex hoc nunc et usque in sæculum.) He serves to obtain the friendship of a person. This genius rules over astronomy and physics; he influences all those who distinguish themselves in this field. They who are born under this influence will love travel, and all honest pleasures; they will have a sensitive heart, and love will cause them sorrows.\n\nThe contrary genius influences libertines, and particularly those who indulge in passions contrary to the order of nature.",
  "62nd. Iah-hel. His attribute (Supreme Being). He corresponds to the name Suna, according to the language of the ancient Carmanians. His ray begins from the 306th degree of the sphere up to the 310th, inclusively, corresponding to the 31st decade and to the genius named Oroasoer. He presides over the following days: 20 May, 31 July, 11 October, 22 December, 4 March. The invocation is made from 8 o'clock 20 minutes in the evening until 8 o'clock 40 minutes; one must pronounce the 159th verse of psalm 118. (Vide quoniam mandata tua dilexi Domine, in misericordia tua vivifica me.) He serves to acquire wisdom. This genius governs philosophers, the illuminated, and all those who wish to withdraw from the world. The person who is born under this influence will love tranquility and solitude; they will exactly fulfill the duties of their station, and they will distinguish themselves by their modesty and their virtues.\n\nThe contrary genius influences all that leads to scandal; he governs luxury, inconstancy, and divorce; he provokes disunion between spouses.",
  "63rd. Anauel ענואל. His attribute is interpreted (God infinitely good). He corresponds to the holy name of God Miri according to the language of the Cambodians. His ray begins from the 311th degree of the sphere up to the 315th, inclusively, corresponding to the 32nd decade and to the genius named Aseü, under the influence of Mercury. He presides over the five following days: 21 May, 1st August, 12 October, 23 December, 5 March. The invocation is made from 8 hours 40 minutes in the evening until precisely 9 o'clock, pronouncing the divine names and the 11th verse of psalm 2. (Servite Domino in timore: et exultate ei cum tremore.) He serves to convert nations to Christianity, and to confound those who are their enemies. This genius protects against accidents; he preserves health and cures sickness; he governs commerce, bankers, business agents and clerks. The person who is born under this influence will have a subtle and ingenious mind; they will be distinguished by their industry and activity.\n\nThe contrary genius governs folly and prodigality; he influences all those who ruin themselves through their bad conduct.",
  "Mehiel כוהיאל. His attribute (God who vivifies all things). He corresponds to the holy name Alli, according to the language of the Mongols. His ray begins from the 316th degree of the sphere up to the 320th, inclusively, corresponding to the 32nd decade and to the genius named Astiro. He presides over the following days: 22 May, 2 August, 13 October, 24 December, 6 March. The invocation is made from 9 o'clock in the evening until 9 o'clock 20 minutes, pronouncing the divine names with the 18th verse of psalm 32. (Ecce oculi Domini super metuentes eum : et in eis, qui sperant super misericordiam ejus.) This psalm is good against adversities; it grants the prayers and wishes of those who hope in the mercy of God. This genius and those that follow, up to the 72nd, belong to the 9th order, which the orthodox call the choir of angels. This genius protects against rabies and ferocious animals; he governs scholars, professors, orators and authors; he has influence over printing and bookselling, and over all those who trade in them. The person who is born under this influence will distinguish themselves in literature.\n\nThe contrary genius governs false scholars; he has influence over controversies, literary disputes and criticism.",
  '65th. Damabiah דמביה. Its attribute (God, fountain of wisdom). He corresponds to the holy name Tara, according to the language of the Gymnosophists. His ray begins from the 321st degree of the sphere up to the 325th, inclusively, corresponding to the 33rd decade and to the genius named Ptébiou, under the influence of the Moon. He presides over the following days: 23 May, 5 August, 14 October, 25 December, 7 March. The invocation is made from 9 hours 20 minutes in the evening until 9 hours 40, pronouncing the 15th verse of psalm 89. (Convertere Domine, et usque quo? et deprecabilis esto super servos tuos.) He serves against sorceries, and to obtain wisdom and the success of useful undertakings.\n\nThis genius governs the seas, the rivers, the springs, maritime expeditions, and naval constructions; he has influence over sailors, pilots, fishing, and those who trade in it. The person who is born under this influence will distinguish themselves in the navy by their expeditions and discoveries, and they will amass a considerable fortune.\n\nThe contrary genius causes storms and shipwrecks; he has influence over unfortunate expeditions.',
  "66th. Manakel .בונקאה. His attribute (God who assists and maintains all things). He corresponds to the name Pora, according to the language of the Brahmans. His ray begins from the 326th degree of the sphere up to the 330th, inclusively, corresponding to the 33rd decade and to the genius named Tépisatras. He presides over the five days following: 24 May, 4 August, 15 October, 26 December, 8 March. The invocation is made from 9 o'clock 40 minutes in the evening until 10 o'clock exactly, reciting the 22nd verse of psalm 37. (Ne derelinquas me Domine Deus meus; ne discesseris à me.) He serves to appease the wrath of God, and to cure epilepsy. He rules over vegetation and over aquatic animals; he influences sleep and dreams. The person who is born under this influence will unite all the fine qualities of body and soul; they will win the friendship and goodwill of all good people through their amiability and the gentleness of their character.\n\nThe contrary genius influences all the bad physical and moral qualities.",
  "Eiael איעאל. His attribute (God, delight of the children of men). He corresponds to the name Bogo, according to the language of the Albanians. His ray begins from the 331st. degree up to the 335th., inclusively, corresponding to the 34th. decade and to the genius named Abiou, under the influence of Saturn. He presides over the following days: 25 May, 6 August, 16 October, 27 December, 9 March. This genius is invoked from 10 o'clock in the evening until 10 o'clock 20 minutes; the request is pronounced with the divine names and the 4th. verse of psalm 36. (Delectare in Domino et dabit tibi petitiones cordis tui.) He serves to obtain consolation in adversities, and to acquire wisdom. This genius governs changes, the preservation of monuments, and longevity of life; he has influence over the occult sciences; he makes the truth known to those who have recourse to him in their labours. The person who is born under this influence will become illuminated by the spirit of God; they will love solitude, and they will distinguish themselves in the higher sciences; principally astronomy, physics and philosophy.\n\nThe contrary genius governs error, prejudices, and those who propagate erroneous systems.",
  'Habuhiah, attribute (God who gives with liberality). He corresponds to the holy name Dépos, according to the language of the Peloponnesians. His ray begins from the 337th degree of the sphere up to the 340th, inclusively, corresponding to the 34th decade and to the genius named Archatapias. He presides over the following days: 26 May, 6 August, 17 October, 28 December, 10 March. The invocation is made from 10 hours 20 minutes in the evening until 10 hours 40, reciting the 1st verse of psalm 105 (Confitemini Domino, quoniam bonus : quoniam in sæculum misericordia ejus.) He serves to preserve health and to cure illnesses. This genius governs agriculture and fecundity. The person who is born under this influence will love the countryside, hunting, gardens, and all that pertains to agriculture.\n\nThe contrary genius governs sterility; it causes famine and plague; it influences the insects that harm the produce of the earth.',
  "69th. Rochel .ראחאל. His attribute (God who sees all).\nHe corresponds to the holy name Déos, according to the language of the Cretans. His ray begins from the 341st degree of the sphere up to the 345th, corresponding to the 35th decade and to the genius named Chontaré, under the influence of Jupiter. He presides over the following days: 27 May, 7 August, 18 October, 29 December, 11 March. The invocation is made from 10 o'clock 40 minutes in the evening until 11 o'clock precisely, pronouncing the 5th verse of psalm 15. (Dominus pars hæreditatis meæ, et calicis mei : tu es, qui restitues hæreditatem meam mihi.) He serves to recover lost or stolen objects, and to know the person who took them. This genius governs fame, fortune and successions; he has influence over jurists, magistrates, attorneys, lawyers and notaries. The person who is born under this influence will distinguish themselves at the bar, with their knowledge of the customs, usages, and spirit of the laws of all peoples.\n\nThe contrary genius governs lawsuits, wills and bequests made to the detriment of the rightful heirs; he has influence over all those who cause the ruin of families, by provoking enormous costs and endless lawsuits.",
  "Jabamiah (1). His attribute (The Word which produces all things). He corresponds to the holy name Aris, according to the language of the Boeotians. His ray begins from the 346th degree of the sphere up to the 350th, inclusively, corresponding to the 35th decade and to the genius named Thopibui. He presides over the following five days: 28 May, 8 August, 19 October, 30 December, 12 March. The invocation is made every day from 11 o'clock in the evening until 11 o'clock 20 minutes. The request must be pronounced with the divine names and the 1st verse of Genesis: (In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth). This genius governs the generation of beings, and the phenomena of nature; he protects those who wish to regenerate themselves, and to re-establish in themselves the harmony that was broken by Adam's disobedience, which is done by exalting oneself toward God, and by purifying through the elements those parts which compose the nature of man: it is then that the wise one returns into the principle of creation; that they recover their rights, their first dignity; that they become again the master of nature, and that they enjoy all the prerogatives which God gave them in creating them. The person who is born under this influence will be distinguished by their genius; they will be esteemed by the learned men of all nations, and they will become one of the foremost lights of philosophy.\n\nThe contrary genius governs atheism, and all those who propagate dangerous writings; it influences critics and literary disputes.\n\n(1) The Abbé de Villars says that this name expresses the eternal fecundity of God (see the Comte de Gabalis, 4th conversation). This work is found in the Recueil des voyages imaginaires et romans cabalistiques, volume 34. The author relates on this subject a singular story: « When Noah wandered upon the avenging waves which flooded the universe, women were then reduced to a small number who saved themselves in the cabalistic ark, which this second father of the world had built; this great man, grieving to see the fearful punishment with which the lord punished the excesses caused by the love Adam had had for his Eve; seeing that Adam had lost his posterity by preferring Eve to the daughters of the elements; Noah, I say, made wise by Adam's fatal example, consented that Vesta, his wife, should give herself to the salamander Oromasis, prince of the fiery substances, and persuaded his three children to likewise yield their three wives to the princes of the three other elements. The universe was in a short time repeopled with men so heroic, so learned, so admirable, that their posterity, dazzled by their virtues, took them for divinities. One of Noah's children, rebellious against his father's counsel, could not resist the attractions of his wife, any more than Adam could resist the charms of his Eve; but as Adam's sin had blackened all the souls of his descendants, the little complaisance that Ham showed toward the sylphs marked all his black posterity; from this comes, our cabalists say, the horrible complexion of the Ethiopians, and of all those hideous peoples who are commanded to dwell beneath the torrid zone, in punishment for the profane ardor of their father. Noah came out of the Ark, and seeing that Vesta, his wife, was only made more beautiful by the commerce she had had with her lover Oromasis, became passionate for her again. Ham, fearing that his father might yet again people the earth with children as black as his Ethiopians, seized his moment, one day when the good old man was full of wine, and castrated him without mercy. Oromasis, whom jealousy did not prevent from pitying the disgrace of his rival, taught his son Zoroaster, otherwise named Japhet, the name of the almighty God which expresses his eternal fecundity: Japhet pronounced it six times, alternately with his brother Shem, walking backwards toward the patriarch, the dreadful name JABAMIAH; and they restored the old man to »",
  '71* Haiaiel הייאל. His attribute (God, master of the universe). He corresponds to the name Zeut, according to the language of the Phrygians. His ray begins from the 351st degree of the sphere up to the 355th, inclusive, corresponding to the 36th decade and to the genius named Ptibiou, under the influence of Mars. He presides over the five days following: 29 May, 9 August, 20 October, 31 December, 14 March. The invocation is made from 11 hours 20 minutes in the evening until 11 hours 40, pronouncing the 29th verse of psalm 108. (Confitebor Domino nimis in ore meo: et in medio multorum laudabo eum.) He serves to confound the wicked, and to deliver oneself from those who wish to oppress us. This genius protects all those who have recourse to him; he gives victory and peace, he has influence over iron, arsenals, cities of war, and all that pertains to the military art. The person who is born under this influence will have much energy; they will love the military life, and will distinguish themselves by their bravery, their talents and their activity.\n\nThe contrary genius rules discord; he has influence over traitors, and over all those who become notorious for their crimes.',
  "72nd Mumiah. כומיה. His attribute is figured by the omega, which designates the end of all things; he rules over Thrace or Roumelia. His ray begins from the 356th degree to the 360th and last degree of the sphere, corresponding to the last decade and to the genius named Atembui. (See the Sacred Calendar, page 41.) He presides over the following days: 30 May, 10 August, 21 October, 1st January, 14 March. The invocation is made from 11 o'clock 40 minutes in the evening until midnight precisely; one must pronounce the divine names, namely alpha and omega, along with the name and attributes of the genius, as well as the request and the 7th verse of psalm 114. (Convertere anima mea in requiem tuam: quia Dominus benefecit tibi.) One must have a talisman which is on the frontispiece, with that of the genius written on the other side, which must be prepared under favourable influences indicated in the chapter on cabalistic Astrology. This genius protects in mysterious operations; he makes one succeed in all things, and brings every experiment to its conclusion; he rules over chemistry, physics and medicine, he influences health and longevity of life. The person who is born under this influence will distinguish themself in medicine; they will become famous for their marvellous cures, will reveal several secrets of nature which will bring happiness to the children of the earth, and they will devote their vigils and their care to relieving the poor and the sick.",
]
